    "narrative": "Today\u2019s outlook for the Austin Waves focuses on maximizing efficiency against Shane Drohan, whose 3.91 xERA suggests a manageable environment for our bats. **Kyle Tucker** headlines our lineup today with a strong 63.81 score. Despite the lineup status being officially pending, his placement in the cleanup spot remains the anchor of our offense. His high floor is driven by consistent recency and a favorable matchup where the SP skill penalty is negligible, allowing his base production to shine. **Andy Pages** also makes the cut at 52.22; while his projection is dampened by a lower spot in the order, his utility value is maintained by a neutral platoon edge, keeping him just above our 50-point start threshold.\n\nThe decision to bench **Liam Hicks** at 38.17 was the most significant deliberation of the session. While his 11% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Williams is promising, the elite 2.95 xERA of the opposing starter created a drag on his raw production that dropped him below our \"Zebras Floor\" of 40.0. Similarly, **Brayan Rocchio** failed to secure a start; his 36.92 score was hampered by a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a difficult matchup against Jax. We are managing our game caps strictly today, prioritizing the higher-probability output of **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** over the lower-upside prospects currently held in reserve. \n\nWe continue to monitor the IL status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose absence leaves a void in our outfield speed production, elevating the importance of our current starters to maintain our standing in the SB category. With **Jackson Merrill** also off the schedule today, our bench remains thin. We are proceeding with caution as the \"Lineup Pending\" status for both **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** introduces a slight risk of last-minute tactical shifts, though we expect no changes to the projected hitting order that would necessitate a change in our roster strategy.",
